The 1923–24 Scottish football season was [[Celtic F.C.|Celtic]]'s 36th season of competitive football, in which they competed in the [[Scottish First Division]]<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.londonhearts.com/scores/a1920/celtic1924.htm|title=Results for Celtic for 1923-24|website=www.londonhearts.com}}</ref> and the [[Scottish Cup]].

In the league, Celtic ended third below Rangers and Airdrieonians, same as the previous year.

In the Scottish Cup, which they entered as champions, they lost 2-0 away to [[Kilmarnock F.C.|Kilmarnock]] in the first round.

This was the last season in which captain [[William Cringan|Willie Cringan]] played for Celtic, as he transferred early in the season to [[Third Lanark A.C.|Third Lanark]].

